  <div class="section" id="home-faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Common Questions</h2>
        <p>Start with low-cost, high-impact moves before bigger changes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">Will an unfavorable door direction always block wealth?</div><div class="faq-a"><p>Not always. Entry flow, light, and storage friction usually matter more first. Optimize those and review outcomes in 7 to 14 days.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">What should I fix first with a limited budget?</div><div class="faq-a"><p>Address one or two high-impact issues first, such as entry congestion, unstable sleep area, or kitchen door-line conflicts.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">Is feng shui optimization worth it for rentals?</div><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Focus on reversible, low-cost changes like movement-path cleanup, layered lighting, and storage improvements.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q">How often should I review after adjustments?</div><div class="faq-a"><p>Review every 7 to 14 days and track sleep, focus, and execution quality. Reassess the plan after four weeks.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

